d:s*1+0.0005*-1+2*r
e:(a*b+c;a+b*c)

=== QP005 profile: uqf | a subtraction left of the multiplication does not make the addition right of it safe
r:a-b*c+d

=== clean profile: every | a qSQL phrase is an expression of its own: `from` and `where` end a run as a comma does
r:select a*b from t where c+d>0
s:select sum size*price by sym from trade where time>start-0D01
u:update v:a%b from t where c-d

=== QP005 QP007 profile: every | and inside one phrase a mix is a mix
r:select mid:0.5*bid+ask, spread:ask-bid from q
s:select from t where a+b*c>0

=== QP005 profile: every | `from` and `where` close nothing where no template is open, nor does a name that ends in one
x:.a.from*1+til 5
f:{[from;to] from*2+to}
w:2*where a+b

=== clean profile: uqf | parenthesised, the order is said out loud
r:(2*3)+4

=== QP005 profile: uqf | in a statement that ends in a semicolon, in a one-line lambda and in brackets (#511)
f:{[a;b;c]
  r:a*b+c;
  r}
g:{[a;b;c] a*b+c}
h:2*3+4;
k:(2*3+4)
m:f[2*3+4;1;2]

